~ start

Linda: Did you plant, dear?

Biff: All right, we had it out. I'm going and I'm not writing anymore.

Linda: I think that's the best way, dear. 'Cause there's no use drawing it out, you'll just never get along.

Willy: ...

Biff: People ask where I am and what I'm doing, you don't know, you don't care. That way it'll be off your mind and you can start brightening up again, all right?

Willy: ...
Willy: There's no necessity to mention the pen at all y'know.

Biff: I've got no appointment, Dad. You're never going to see what I am, so what's the use of arguing? If I strike oil, I'll send you a check. Meantime, forget I'm alive.

Willy: Spite, see? May you rot in hell if you leave this house! 
Willy: I want you to know, on the train, in the mountains, in the valleys, wherever you go, that you cut down your life for spite!

Biff: No, no...

Willy: Spite, spite, is the word of your undoing! And when you're down and out, remember what did it. 
Willy: When you're rotting somewhere beside the railroad tracks, remember, and don't you dare blame it on me!

Biff: I'm not blaming you!

Willy: I won't take the rap for this, you hear!?

Happy: You cut it out now!

Biff: The man don't know who we are! The man is gonna know!

Linda: *sobbing*

Biff: Stop crying. I'm through with it.

Willy: Then hang yourself! For spite, hang yourself! The door of your life is wide open!

Biff: Pop! I'm a dime a dozen, and so are you!

Willy: I am not a dime a dozen! I am Willy Loman and you are Biff Loman!

Biff: *breaking* Pop, I'm nothing! I'm nothing, Pop. Can't you understand that? There's no spite in it anymore.

Willy: Linda, why is he crying?

Linda: He loves you Willy!

Happy: Always did, Pop.

Willy: *crying* He cried! Cried to me. That boy is magnificent!

Ben: Yes, outstanding, with twenty thousand behind him.

Linda: Now come to bed, Willy. It's all settled now.

Willy: Yes, we'll sleep. Come on. Go to sleep, Hap.

Ben: And it does take a great kind of a man to crack the jungle...

Happy: I'm getting married, Pop, and don't you forget it. I'm gonna change everything. I'm gonna run that department store.















=> END